Replaces GitHub's automatic Jekyll 'pages build and deployment' — which failed on the first attempt 4/4 times with the transient 'Deployment failed, try again later' and needed a manual re-run every time — with a controlled Actions workflow:

- concurrency group 'pages' serializes deploys so a new push never collides with an in-flight deployment (the usual cause of that error);
- the deploy step auto-retries once, so a transient failure self-heals with no manual re-run;
- stages a clean web root (excludes android/tests/docs/etc.) + .nojekyll so there's no Jekyll build step at all.

ONE-TIME SETUP REQUIRED: repo Settings -> Pages -> Source -> 'GitHub Actions'. Until that's set, GitHub keeps using the old auto-deploy and this workflow will error.


