Adds a full modular policy engine to `intentos-kernel` — the governed syscall evaluation layer that produces structured evidence, multi-rule decisions, and full explainability for every syscall.

## Core types

- **`Evidence`** — 15-variant enum covering scope match/mismatch, quota headroom/exceeded, TTL, token validity, sandbox isolation, and federation trust
- **`PolicyRule`** — `(id, description, fn(&VerifiedToken, &IkSyscall) -> PolicyResult)` — pure, stateless, zero-allocation
- **`RuleRegistry`** — ordered append-only rule collection; evaluation order is registration order
- **`IkpeDecision`** — `allow`, collected `evidence`, `rule_chain` (inspector trace), `deny_reason`

## Rule modules

| Module | Rules |
|---|---|
| A — Scope | `FsScopeRule`, `NetScopeRule`, `AiScopeRule`, `CompositeScopeRule` |
| B — Quota/TTL | `MaxBytesRule`, `MaxRequestsRule`, `TTLRule` |
| C — Token | `TokenExpiryRule`, `TokenSignatureRule`†, `TokenRevocationRule`† |
| D — Sandbox | `SandboxModeRule` (evidence), `SandboxIsolationRule` (blocks net/AI from `sandbox:` principals) |
| E — Federation | `RemoteKernelTrustRule`†, `PolicyHashConsistencyRule`† |
| F — Custom | `AppPolicyModule` trait + `register_app_module()` |

† skeleton — enforcement already upstream or pending federation registry

## Evaluator

Short-circuits on first denial; accumulates evidence on allow path:

```rust
pub fn evaluate(registry: &RuleRegistry, token: &VerifiedToken, syscall: &IkSyscall) -> IkpeDecision {
    for rule in &registry.rules {
        match (rule.evaluate)(token, syscall) {
            PolicyResult::Allow { evidence: ev } => evidence.extend(ev),
            PolicyResult::Deny { reason, evidence: ev } => {
                // short-circuit, append RuleApplied evidence
                return IkpeDecision { allow: false, … };
            }
        }
    }
    IkpeDecision { allow: true, … }
}
```

## Integration

`dispatch_call` now requires a `&RuleRegistry` (built once at boot via `build_default_registry()`, not per-call) and runs the policy engine before any syscall executes. The default stack has 11 rules ordered cheapest-gate-first.

All public types re-exported from `lib.rs`. 93 tests pass (up from 54).
